        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "351bb8c5-0f52-5bf7-bdcd-8a228f50b97d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dal Lake, Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, Waterton Lake, Alberta, Montana\n- Products: Shikara\n- Structures: Goathaunt Bunkhouse\n\nFacts:\n- Dal Lake is a lake in Srinagar, the summer capital of Jammu and Kashmir.\n- In Kashmiri, “Dal” means “lake,” so “Dal Lake” is a misnomer.\n- Waterton Lake is a mountain lake in southern Alberta, Canada, and northern Montana, United States.\n- The shikara is a type of wooden boat found on Dal Lake and other water bodies of Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, India.\n- Goathaunt Bunkhouse is near the southern end of Waterton Lake.\n- Goathaunt Bunkhouse is the last surviving structure of its era at that location.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fe2e9792-cd3f-53c6-a092-83762773428f",
        "text": "Page: Dal Lake. Sentence: Dal is a lake in Srinagar (Dal Lake is a misnomer as Dal in Kashmiri means lake), the summer capital of Jammu and Kashmir.\nPage: Waterton Lake. Sentence: Waterton Lake is a mountain lake in southern Alberta, Canada and northern Montana, United States.\nPage: Shikara. Sentence: The shikara is a type of wooden boat found on Dal Lake and other water bodies of Srinagar, Jammu & Kashmir, India.\nPage: Goathaunt Bunkhouse. Sentence: The bunkhouse is the last surviving structure of this era at this location, near the southern end of Waterton Lake.",
